From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 04:18:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: configs: asahi: keep the kernel console in
 pstore

The J604 device tree now reserves a ramoops region. With
CONFIG_PSTORE_CONSOLE the console written before a hard reset is kept
there and can be read on the next boot from /sys/fs/pstore. That is the
only kernel trail a watchdog reset leaves when the journal has not been
flushed, as in the T8132 suspend-to-RAM bring-up.

CONFIG_PSTORE and CONFIG_PSTORE_RAM are already enabled; nothing is
recorded unless a ramoops region exists.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 arch/arm64/configs/asahi.config | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/asahi.config b/arch/arm64/configs/asahi.config
index 0a5f6bc6cc..659e4b13b6 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/asahi.config
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/asahi.config
@@ -157,6 +157,7 @@ CONFIG_UDMABUF=y
 CONFIG_DETECT_HUNG_TASK=y
 CONFIG_EDAC=y
 CONFIG_EDAC_APPLE_SOC=m
+CONFIG_PSTORE_CONSOLE=y
 # Confine kernel executable code to a fixed physical CTXR window so the kernel
 # can run at EL2 on chips whose firmware locks the code-execute range. Inert
 # unless the bootloader supplies a window (/chosen/aurora,ctxr-exec-window) or
